cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arabicwer, please cite it as below and name the policy you scored with, for example WER (arabicwer-1/lenient)."
type: software
title: "arabicwer: Arabic WER and CER under named, versioned normalisation policies"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bayanat-Labs/arabicwer"
authors:
  - name: "Bayanat Labs"
keywords:
  - arabic
  - speech-recognition
  - asr-evaluation
  - word-error-rate
  - character-error-rate
  - text-normalization
abstract: "A Python package, command line, specification and browser page for Arabic word and character error rates under six named, immutable, hash-identified normalisation policies (arabicwer-1: raw, nfc, dediac, strict-orth, bayanat-norm-v1, lenient), with conformance fixtures, a deterministic alignment rule and a case study on FLEURS Egyptian Arabic."
